                    ***                   - Lucas Visscher            ***
                    ***                   - Xiang Yuan                ***
                    ***                                               ***
                    ***  Features:        - CCD/CC2/CCSD              ***
                    ***                   - Higher-order CC methods   ***
                    ***                   - Frozen virtual NOs        ***
                    ***                   - 1RDM CCD/CCSD, 2RDM CCSD  ***
                    ***                   - CIS and CIS(D)            ***
                    ***                   - EOM-CCSD                  ***
                    ***                   - LR and QR CCSD            ***
                    ***                   - ReSpect interface         ***
                    ***                                               ***
                    ***  Relativistic Coupled Cluster code using      ***
                    ***  CPU and GPU-accelerated tensor libraries :   ***
                    ***                                               ***
                    ***  - TALSH and ExaTensor libraries developed by ***
                    ***  Dmitry Lyakh (see doi: 10.1002/qua.25926)    ***
                    ***  - Backends supported by the Tensor Agebra    ***
                    ***  Processing Primitives (TAPP) API (see TAPP   ***
                    ***  whitepaper https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.07827) ***
                    ***                                               ***
                    *****************************************************
 
 References
 
  - Ground-state CCD/CC2/CCSD/CCSD(T) energies, CCD/CCSD expectation values:
     JV Pototschnig et al., J. Chem. Theory Comput. 17, 5509 (2021).
     doi: 10.1021/acs.jctc.1c00260
 
  - MP2 virtual frozen natural orbitals, generation of CC natural orbitals:
     X Yuan, L Visscher, ASP Gomes, J. Chem. Phys. 156, 224108 (2022). 
     doi: 10.1063/5.0087243
 
  - Virtual frozen natural orbitals for response properties:
     M Le, X Yuan, ASP Gomes, in preparation
 
  - Equation of motion coupled cluster (EOM-CCSD) for IP, EE and EA:
     X Yuan, PhD thesis, Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam and Universite de Lille
     doi: 10.5463/thesis.505
 
  - (EOM-)CCSD 1RDMs and CCSD 2RDM
     L Halbert, ASP Gomes, in preparation
 
  - CIS and CIS(D) excitation energies and transition moments
     X Yuan, T Lejeune, ASP Gomes, in preparation
 
  - Orbital-unrelaxed linear response (EOM-)CCSD theory:
     X Yuan et al., J. Chem. Theory Comput. (2024). 
     doi: 10.1021/acs.jctc.3c00812
 
  - Orbital-unrelaxed quadratic response (EOM-)CCSD theory:
     X Yuan, L Halbert, L Visscher, ASP Gomes, J. Chem. Theory Comput. 19, 9248 (2023). 
     doi: 10.1021/acs.jctc.3c01011
     X Yuan, L Halbert, L Visscher, ASP Gomes, J. Phys. Chem. A 129, 11695 (2025). 
     doi: 10.1021/acs.jpca.5c04475
 
  - Higher-order coupled cluster methods
   - code generated with the Tenpi framework (https://gitlab.com/janbrandejs/tenpi)
     - ground-state energies (CCSDT, CCSDTQ) 
       J Brandejs, J Pototschnig, T Saue, J. Chem. Theory Comput. 21, 7320 (2025). 
       doi: 10.1021/acs.jctc.5c00219
     - ground-state expectation values (CCSDT, CCSDTQ) 
       G Fabbro, J Brandejs, T Saue, J. Phys. Chem. A 129, 6942 (2025). 
       doi: 10.1021/acs.jpca.5c02844
   - code generated with the mb-autogen framework (doi: 10.5281/zenodo.8094429)
     - ground-state energies (CCSDT/-1a/-1b/-2/-3, CCSDTQ, CCSDTQP) 
       L Halbert, ASP Gomes, in preparation
 
